### Future Directives
- **RAG Integrity**: All documentation in `docs/` and `memlog/` must be synchronized for embedding after every major change.
- **Continuous Documentation**: [walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/kirkl/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2902aaa3-379c-4c29-9bc9-e2194680c099/walkthrough.md) is a living chronological document; DO NOT create new walkthroughs for sub-tasks, always append.
- Implement true multi-camera stereoscopic depth mapping.
- Extend the "Trace Route" to include audio driver health and lattice VAD status.

### 5. Advanced Audit & Traceability
- **Hardware Trace Route**: Added a live console to the Audit panel that traces WMI enumeration and index probing in real-time.
- **Forced Sync**: Opening the audit screen now triggers a [refresh_hardware()](file:///d:/Projects/impressioncore/src/orchestrator/orbcloud_vision.py#990-1023) call that re-initializes all camera objects and updates the system device tree.
- **Debug Inclusion**: The "hw_trace" is now permanently part of the JSON debug snapshot for deep troubleshooting.

#### Trace Route Live View:
![Audit Trace Route](file:///C:/Users/kirkl/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2902aaa3-379c-4c29-9bc9-e2194680c099/final_audit_panel_state_1766893617243.png)

### 6. Bug Fixes (Hot-Swap & Feeds)
- **Standardized Virtual IDs**: Fixed an inconsistency where PS Eye cameras were indexed at 100+ but the API logic expected 99. They now start at 99 for immediate detection.
- **Stale Frame Clearing**: Implemented logic to clear the visual buffer during a hardware refresh, preventing frozen or black frames from appearing during the re-probe.
- **Process Contention**: Identified and documented a conflict caused by multiple background instances which was locking the camera hardware.

### 7. Graceful Lifecycle Management
- **Startup Protection**: Updated [orbos_ready.bat](file:///d:/Projects/impressioncore/orbos_ready.bat) to automatically terminate lingering backend/frontend processes. No more "address already in use" or "hardware lock" errors.
- **Graceful Shutdown**: Added a dedicated `/v1/system/shutdown` endpoint and a **SHUTDOWN SYSTEM** button to the Audit Overlay. This releases all camera/audio resources before exiting.
- **Documentation Audit**: Completed a 24h ledger of all changes, including [change_log.md](file:///C:/Users/kirkl/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2902aaa3-379c-4c29-9bc9-e2194680c099/change_log.md) and [memlog.md](file:///C:/Users/kirkl/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2902aaa3-379c-4c29-9bc9-e2194680c099/memlog.md).

## Verification Results
- **Startup**: System launches in ~3 seconds via [orbos_ready.bat](file:///d:/Projects/impressioncore/orbos_ready.bat). Multiple calls correctly terminate the previous instance.
- **UI**: Initialize button enables automatically. Shutdown button successfully halts the system.
- **Audit**: Accurate microphone count and PnP inventory. Trace Route shows clear discovery path.
- **Refresh**: Plugging/unplugging cameras is detected immediately upon opening the audit screen.

## Updated Architecture
The [UnifiedBrainTriad](file:///d:/Projects/impressioncore/src/orchestrator/unified_triad.py#25-740) now acts as a true central orchestrator, managing the lifecycle of both sensory inputs (Vision/Audio) and maintaining system health.
